  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe overall pattern that we have been in for the past week will \nlikely remain steadfast through the next week. Strong upper level \nridging will not budge much and with a strong surface high over the \nSE US, offshore flow keeps moisture away. A couple of weak cold \nfronts make their way under the ridge this week. The first one is \nMonday, which will slightly increase clouds and the winds, followed \nby a slightly cooler Tuesday. Models are hinting at some light rain \nalong the front but soundings are very dry so precipitation chances \nwere kept below 15%. Next front does not look to come through till \nearly next weekend with also a similar story, slight decrease in \ntemps and an increase in winds and high clouds briefly.\n\nWith this dry pattern and a couple days with stronger winds with dry \nfrontal passages and now most of the leaves are off the trees, fire \ndanger is increasing. With continued drying it will become easier \nfor fires to spread. Luckily even on our windiest days this week, \npeak downward momentum transfer in forecast soundings is around 20 \nmph Monday and Tuesday.",
